content.text:
The only fault is ts-route-service: its pod stopped serving at about 04:22:35 and never recovered, and the user-facing dashboard's route calls failed as a result. I checked the errors and latencies across all services and found none outside ts-ui-dashboard and the load generator.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-route-service",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, metric, attr_k8s_pod_name pod, round(value,1) v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.memory.rss','container.memory.rss','container.cpu.usage') ORDER BY time LIMIT 20", "claim": "Route-service pod memory RSS collapsed from about 825 MB to about 344 KB at 04:22:39 and stayed there."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) m, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "Route-service emits spans only in the first abnormal minute (59 spans), then none for the rest of the window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name='GET /api/v1/routeservice/routes' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ui-dashboard's GET /routeservice/routes returned 118 HTTP 503 errors averaging about 3.5 s."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "ts-route-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
     "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) m, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_http_response_status_code>=500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "ui-dashboard errors on route requests rise from the first abnormal minute, about 14 to 30 per minute, while route-service is silent."}]}
  ]
}
```

